    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §52-0908, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9547\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\nproviding an exemption from requirements for the alienation of parkland\nfor renewable energy generating projects in the county of Westchester\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to provide an exemption from require-\nments for the alienation of parkland for certain renewable energy gener-\nating projects in Westchester County only.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSECTION 1. A new section 52-0908 is added to the Environmental Conserva-\ntion Law: RESTRICTION ON ALIENATION EXEMPTION IN WESTCHESTER COUNTY;\nRENEWABLE ENERGY GENERATING PROJECTS. This will allow for the alienation\nof certain parklands within Westchester County without going to the\nstate legislature. This applies solely to the airspace directly above\nreal property located in the county of Westchester, that was used for\nvehicle parking prior to the effective date of this section, and only\nfor the purpose of constructing, installing and/or operating solar ener-\ngy project that will not exceed two megawatts of generating capacity.\n\nSECTION 2. Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnder current law, municipalities must request an act from the legisla-\nture to alienate parklands, including the airspace directly above real\nproperty that is being used for vehicle parking. As New York State looks\nfor ways to implement the Climate Act, interest in solar projects in the\nairspace above vehicle parking has increased.  Solar panels are known as\na source of cleaner, renewable energy, which provides cost savings and\ngenerates revenue.\n\nThis bill will bypass the procedure of requesting an act from the Legis-\nlature when allowing solar energy projects under 2 megawatts to be\nlocated directly above real property that is currently being used for\nvehicle parking, resulting in certain solar projects being replicated\nmore efficiently, saving time and further reducing our carbon footprint.\nThis legislation was requested by the county of Westchester and\nsupported by municipalities within.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTBD\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall apply to alienations of\nparkland for renewable energy generating projects in the county of West-\nchester occurring on or after that date.\n",
