    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9547A\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\nproviding an exemption from requirements for the alienation of parkland\nfor renewable energy generating projects in the county of Westchester\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to provide an exemption from require-\nments for the alienation of parkland for certain renewable energy gener-\nating projects in Westchester County only.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSECTION 1. A new section 52-0908 is added to the Environmental Conserva-\ntion Law:\n\nRESTRICTION ON ALIENATION EXEMPTION IN WESTCHESTER COUNTY; RENEWABLE\nENERGY GENERATING PROJECTS. This will allow for the alienation of\ncertain parklands within Westchester County without going to the state\nlegislature. This applies solely to the airspace directly above real\nproperty located in the county of Westchester, that was used for vehicle\nparking prior to the effective date of this section, and only for the\npurpose of constructing, installing and/or operating solar energy\nproject that will not exceed two megawatts of generating capacity.\n\nSECTION 2. Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnder current law, local governments must request an act from the legis-\nlature to alienate parklands, including the airspace directly above real\nproperty that is being used for vehicle parking. As New York State looks\nfor ways to implement the Climate Act, interest in solar projects in the\nairspace above vehicle parking has increased.  Solar panels are known as\na source of cleaner, renewable energy, which provides cost savings and\ngenerates revenue.  This bill will bypass the procedure of requesting an\nact from the Legislature when allowing solar energy projects under 2\nmegawatts to be located directly above real property that is currently\nbeing used for vehicle parking, resulting in certain solar projects\nbeing replicated more efficiently, saving time and further reducing our\ncarbon footprint. This legislation was requested by the county of West-\nchester.   \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall apply to alienations of\nparkland for renewable energy generating projects in the county of West-\nchester occurring on or after that date.\n",
